# Copy to config.env and edit. Every setting has a working default, so an empty
# config.env (or none at all) is fine for a first run.
#
# config.env is gitignored.

# The macOS account that runs the model server and owns its API key. Defaults to
# whoever runs the scripts (or ran `sudo`). The server runs while this account
# is logged in.
#LLM_USER=

# The model, as Splash's --model takes it: an MLX repository, or a GGUF
# repository and variant, OWNER/REPO:VARIANT (for example
# unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_M). Splash serves Qwen3.8-27B and
# Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, downloads the model at its first start, and pairs the draft
# model trained for it by itself. Choosing a model is covered in README.md,
# "Choose a model". It is also the model ID clients use, so changing it means
# changing every client's config.
#LLM_MODEL=mlx-community/Qwen3.8-27B-4bit

# Tailscale tag applied to this machine. The tailnet policy
# (config/tailscale-policy.hujson) grants access by this tag.
#LLM_TAG=tag:llm-server

# SSH hardening, applied only if Remote Login is on. "yes" refuses SSH from
# anything outside the tailnet (100.64.0.0/10) in addition to disabling
# passwords. Set "no" to keep LAN SSH, key-only.
#LLM_SSH_TAILNET_ONLY=yes

# Laptops only. Shut down cleanly on battery at or below this percentage,
# instead of running flat and losing everything.
#LLM_BATTERY_SHUTDOWN_PCT=15

# Laptops only. "yes" runs `pmset -a disablesleep 1`, which keeps a laptop
# serving with the lid shut. It is system-wide (battery too) and undocumented
# in `man pmset`; verified on mains power only -- see README.md.
#LLM_DISABLE_SLEEP=no
